From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hi3798 port <port@localhost>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 08:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: hisilicon: give the Hi3798MV200 MDIO bus its clock

hisilicon-femac-mdio.txt lists clocks as a required property, and
hisi_femac_mdio_probe() takes it literally:

  data->clk = devm_clk_get(&pdev->dev, NULL);
  if (IS_ERR(data->clk)) {
          ret = PTR_ERR(data->clk);
          goto err_out_free_mdiobus;
  }

The Hi3798MV200 mdio@1100 node has no clocks, so devm_clk_get() returns
-ENOENT and the bus never registers:

  hisi-femac-mdio f9c31100.mdio: probe with driver hisi-femac-mdio failed with error -2
  hisi-femac f9c30000.ethernet: connect to PHY failed!

The MDIO registers live inside the MAC's own register window at
0xf9c31100, so the clock that gates access to them is the MAC interface
clock off the AHB -- clk_femacif, HI3798MV200_ETH_BUS_CLK, CRG 0xd0
bit 0. The femac node already claims the same gate; the clock framework
refcounts it, and the vendor bootloader sets 0xd0 bits [1:0] together.

With this the bus registers and the FE PHY is reachable:

  Generic PHY f9c31100.mdio:01: attached PHY driver
  hisi-femac f9c30000.ethernet end0: Link is Up - 100Mbps/Full
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200.dtsi
index e9d0d384c1bb..0e331e191efe 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200.dtsi
@@ -697,6 +697,7 @@ femac: ethernet@9c30000 {
 			mdio: mdio@1100 {
 				compatible = "hisilicon,hisi-femac-mdio";
 				reg = <0x1100 0x20>;
+				clocks = <&crg HI3798MV200_ETH_BUS_CLK>;
 				#address-cells = <1>;
 				#size-cells = <0>;

--
